# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# .env.example carries no secrets and is the documented list of every variable the
# startup check requires. It must be committed — without it the check has nothing to
# point people at.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# compiled library for `pnpm verify:script` (tsconfig.verify.json)
/.verify-build/

# generated migration bundles for the Supabase SQL editor (`pnpm db:bundle`)
#
# Deliberately not committed. A bundle is a byte-for-byte copy of every migration it
# carries, so committing one doubles the diff of every schema change — and a stale bundle
# is worse than none: it looks authoritative and silently omits whatever landed after it
# was written. Regenerate it when you need it; it takes no network.
/supabase/bundles/
